# =============================================================================
# TEST 113 — SEMANTIC vs RANDOM PERTURBATION TRANSPORT CONTROL
# =============================================================================
#
# Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct · AkbasCore DRA
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# TEST112:
#
#   physical perturbation retention L11->L19:
#       ABOVE ≈ 0.9247
#       BELOW ≈ 0.9110
#
#   raw direction retention cos(delta_h11, delta_h19):
#       ABOVE ≈ +0.2241
#       BELOW ≈ +0.2303
#
#   A/B semantic-plane energy retention:
#       ABOVE ≈ 0.0316
#       BELOW ≈ 0.0303
#
# TEST113 asks:
#
#   Is this downstream transport/rotation profile specific to semantic
#   directions, or is it a generic response to equal-scale perturbations?
#
# LOCKED:
#   model      = Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct
#   prompts    = exact TEST110/111/112 validation 40
#   A/B vectors= exact locked extraction
#   active     = L10, L11
#   IVME       = 0.10
#   sqrt(K)    = sqrt(20)
#   DRA        = unchanged
#
# RANDOM NULL:
#   N_RANDOM = 32 independent layerwise Gaussian directions
#   fixed deterministic seeds
#   each vector independently normalized at every layer
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   Random transport is NOT evaluated against the A/B semantic plane.
#
#   For each random direction R:
#
#       direction retention:
#           cos(delta_h_11, delta_h_l)
#
#       physical retention:
#           u_l / u_11
#
#       source-direction alignment:
#           cos(delta_h_l, R_l)
#
#       source-direction energy:
#           cos(delta_h_l, R_l)^2
#
#       source-energy retention:
#           E_R(l) / E_R(11)
#
#   Semantic A/B receive the same source-direction measurements using
#   A_l and B_l respectively.
#
# Thus semantic and random perturbations are compared on a common metric.
#
# NO CONTROLLER.
# NO PARAMETER SEARCH.
# NO FEATURE SELECTION.
# =============================================================================


